              "The platform assigns each tenant group a dense allocation index—the smallest unoccupied integer in a bounded range, a first-fit policy over the index set—and derives its entire ingress fan-out from that number by pure arithmetic. Four public port families result: SSH and web NodePorts on the cluster node (31000+idx and 32000+idx), and SSH and web ports published on the relay (22000+idx and 23000+idx). A browser connection to the relay's public web port traverses four hops: TLS terminates at a relay-side reverse proxy that proxies to a loopback port (13000+idx) where the tunnel server listens; the tunnel carries the session to the node, which forwards to the NodePort and onward to the container port. The ten-thousand offset between public and tunnel-internal ports exists because the TLS hop occurs on the same relay host as the tunnel server, so the two port families must not collide; the offset is arbitrary but fixed, and its fixity is what makes the whole scheme auditable by arithmetic.",
              "The decisive property of this scheme is that configuration becomes generation rather than editing. Three independently managed surfaces—the cluster's NodePort Services, the tunnel client's proxy table, and the relay's reverse-proxy configuration—must agree for any port chain to function, and any hand-edited divergence among them is invisible until a connection fails. The platform rewrites each surface from a single authoritative state file into marker-delimited blocks: a managed block in the tunnel client's configuration is regenerated wholesale on every group mutation, one TCP proxy segment per group binding the local NodePort to the relay-side internal port, after which the client is reloaded through its admin API so that new mappings take effect without dropping established tunnels. On the relay, one TLS-enabled server block per group is regenerated with WebSocket upgrade headers and long proxy timeouts appropriate for interactive sessions. A third layer maintains subdomain-to-port virtual-host mappings, editing the relay proxy's configuration over SSH within a fixed marker section, with syntax validation before activation and automatic rollback to the pre-edit copy if validation fails.",
